From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the guest's pointer layer over every display's window

What: with "Pointer on its own layer" (ADR 0054) each window of another
display (OmacVMHeadView) gets a pointer layer, as the main window has its
cursor layer: the image of that output's cursor plane (copied,
premultiplied as virtio-gpu sends it), at the plane's top left, scaled as
the window stretches the output's frames (ui/omacvm-pointer-heads.h),
above the frames, shown while the guest shows the plane. Kept per output
on the main thread, so a window made again shows the pointer as it is. The
hidden macPointer keeps its own way (the Mac's cursor shows the image).

Why: the guest's driver now gives every output a cursor plane and the
guest draws no pointer into any output's frames. Before, only output 0
had a plane and QEMU only showed the main window's; the other outputs
were meant to keep Hyprland's software pointer, but aquamarine 0.15.1
takes a cursor for an output without a plane without an error, so
Hyprland drew none there either: no pointer at all on an external display
(#554). The cursor commands already carry the output (scanout id): each
output's console gets its own.

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's display windows).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-pointer-heads.sh (the rules; the
wiring on the patched ui/cocoa.m; --self-test: every wiring check fails on
the code without it).
